En de cruciale semantische scheiding blijft:

Cryptographic authenticity
          ≠
Epistemic truth
          ≠
Constitutional authority
          ≠
Operational safety

Een geldige signature betekent dus uitsluitend dat de geassocieerde sleutelhouder de exacte canonical representation heeft ondertekend.

Implementation contract

De crate krijgt minimaal deze publieke API:

pub struct ContentDigest(pub [u8; 32]);

pub struct KeyId(pub String);

pub struct SignatureBytes(pub Vec<u8>);

pub enum SignatureAlgorithm {
    Ed25519,
}

pub enum CryptographicStatus {
    Unsigned,
    Verified,
    Invalid,
    UnknownKey,
    UnsupportedAlgorithm,
}

pub struct SignedProvenance {
    pub key_id: KeyId,
    pub algorithm: SignatureAlgorithm,
    pub digest: ContentDigest,
    pub signature: SignatureBytes,
    pub signed_at: DateTime<Utc>,
    pub schema_version: String,
}

met:

pub trait CanonicalEncode {
    fn canonical_bytes(&self) -> Vec<u8>;
}

en afzonderlijke:

Signer
Verifier
KeyRing

capabilities.

Tests die verplicht worden

✓ valid signature verifies
✓ mutated payload fails
✓ mutated signature fails
✓ wrong public key fails
✓ digest mismatch detected
✓ unknown key is not "verified"
✓ retired key remains historically identifiable
✓ revoked key follows current policy
✓ canonical encoding is deterministic
✓ NaN / Infinity cannot enter signed numeric domains
✓ signature validity does not produce EvidenceState::Validated
✓ signature validity does not produce Authority
✓ no unsafe PALACO code

Design Freeze

PIS-IND-RIP-334.4A

> Cryptographic verification establishes authenticity and integrity of a canonical record representation; all claims beyond that boundary require independent epistemic and constitutional evaluation.



Dat maakt 334.4A een echte provenance primitive, geen verkapte authority engine.

